From ba73782e22b27f8eb45384e9c0f27c5ab485888a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aee-gfx-buildserver <aee-gfx-buildserver@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Apr 2023 10:36:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] Perfetto: Modify to make perfetto and AGI run ok

Ported from Intel A17 25.0.1 (a7cd4efcc3a) to Mesa 26.0.8:

 - Link Android's libperfetto_client_experimental (and its
   perfetto_flags_c_lib), the way AOSP external/mesa3d does, and configure
   with -Dperfetto=true -Dandroid-libperfetto=enabled (upstream option
   since 25.3). The generated perfetto.pc only satisfies meson's
   dependency lookup. No copy of the perfetto SDK is carried.
 - Install upstream's Android libgpudataproducer.so (exports start(),
   loaded by /system/bin/gpu_counter_producer) as the
   'libgpudataproducer' vendor module. The Intel pps-producer wrapper
   executable and libpps-producer are no longer needed.
 - AGI validation: non-zero submission ids and non-null command buffer
   handles in render stage / submission events (intel_ds_end_submit()
   gains a cmd_buf argument; iris, anv and hasvk callers updated).
 - Android: initialize perfetto lazily from util_perfetto_trace_begin()
   instead of util_cpu_trace_init(), which runs while zygote preloads
   the GL driver and would spawn a thread there, hanging zygote.
 - Recreate IntelPerf per DRM device in init_perfcnt() for multi-GPU
   (iGPU + dGPU) systems.

Dropped because upstream now provides them: GpuCounterDescriptor
registration at data source registration time, and the pps-producer
Android entry point.

Tracked-On: OAM-110834
Signed-off-by: chenyanxzhu <chenyanx.zhu@intel.com>
(cherry picked from commit a7cd4efcc3a11b5e32c9f415c796ee7cf024589e)
Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
